title: Stepping on hex maps
intro: Grid movers now step from hexagon to hexagon, six ways, and tactics units walk and fight over hex maps.
project: Empty | Hex Steps

# A hex field: a floor that doesn't collide, and a layer of walls round it with a pillar in the middle. Cell x, y's
# middle is at (-4.25 + x + half a tile on odd rows, 2 - three quarters of a tile a row).
create: Tilemap
rename: Field
set: Transform.Position = -4.75, 2.5, 0
set: Tilemap.Shape = Hex
set: Tilemap.Tint = #6FA860
set: Tilemap.Tiles = 111111111\n111111111\n111111111\n111111111\n111111111\n111111111
set: Tilemap.Solid = false
click: tiles:layer:+
rename: Walls
set: Tilemap.Tint = #8A8178
set: Tilemap.Tiles = 222222222\n2.......2\n2...2...2\n2.......2\n2.......2\n222222222
set: Tilemap.Solid = true
expecttile: Walls 4, 2 = 2
expecttile: Walls 3, 2 = -1
look: 0, 0, 3.5

chapter: Six ways | Grid Movement on a hex map
deselect
create: Grid Player
set: Transform.Position = -1.75, -0.25, 0
expectat: Player = -1.75, -0.25
explain: world:-5, 2.75, 5, -2.5 | A hex map | Here's a hex map with walls round it and a pillar in the middle, and a grid player. On a hex map, a grid player now steps from hexagon to hexagon.
play
wait: 0.5
expectat: Player = -1.75, -0.25
tap: Right
wait: 0.4
expectat: Player = -0.75, -0.25
say: Left and right step along the row.
hold: Up+Left 0.05
wait: 0.4
expectat: Player = -1.25, 0.5
explain: game | Up and to one side | Up with left or right held steps to the hexagon up on that side.
tap: Up
wait: 0.4
expectat: Player = -0.75, 1.25
tap: Down
wait: 0.4
expectat: Player = -1.25, 0.5
tap: Down
wait: 0.4
expectat: Player = -0.75, -0.25
explain: game | Straight up and down | Up or down alone zigzags between the two hexagons above or below, so holding it walks straight up or down the screen.
hold: Up+Right 0.05
wait: 0.4
expectat: Player = -0.75, -0.25
explain: game | Walls | The pillar is up to the right, so stepping that way bumps into it. Chasers, patrols, crates and turns all step over the hexagons the same way.
stop

chapter: Tactics on hexagons | Reach and range in hexagons
select: Player
key: Delete
deselect
create: Tactics Unit
rename: Knight
set: Transform.Position = -2.25, 0.5, 0
create: Tactics Unit
rename: Orc
set: Transform.Position = 1.25, -0.25, 0
expectat: Knight = -2.25, 0.5
expectat: Orc = 1.25, -0.25
say: Now a knight for Blue and an orc for Red, which the computer plays.
play
wait: 0.6
gameclick: Knight
wait: 0.4
explain: game | Lit as hexagons | Picking the knight lights the hexagons it can walk to in blue, counted in steps round the pillar, and the ones it could hit from them in red.
gameclick: Orc
wait: 1.6
expectvalue: Orc.Health.Current = 2
explain: game | Walk up and strike | Clicking the orc walks the knight round the pillar, a hexagon at a time, into one of the six hexagons next to it, and hits it.
wait: 2
expectvalue: Knight.Health.Current = 2
say: Then the computer's orc hits back from where it stands. Tactics, turns and grid movement now all work on hex maps.
stop
